positions.text:
Entry in "positions":
{keys}
Rights translate into access: leading — "admin" in one's own unit and in all below it (and holds the other positions of the unit, so it can give their links); accompanying — reads one's own unit and all below it; cooperating and membership — write in one's own unit; participation — reads.

fields.text:
Entry in "fields" — a person field (e.g. voice, formation stage, diet):
{keys}
A field with "options" can split a unit into subgroups by itself ("structure.subgroups": "byField", "structure.byField": "glos").

units.text:
Unit ("unit" and every entry in "units"):
{keys}
Moving a unit = the same "key" in another place of the tree: the import moves the area (the importing person leads both places); it also changes the access computed from the tree (leaders above, accompanying, “units below see this one”).

settings.body:
"settings": { "life": { … }, "structure": { … }, "intake": { … }, "tools": { … }, "talk": { … }, "visibility": { … }, "public": { … } }. Step 3 (who does what) is the unit's "positions" and "persons".
{lines}
A value set in the unit wins; without it — from its blueprint; without that — from the unit above (its value, blueprint …); finally the suggestion.

persons.text:
Entry in "persons":
{keys}
Every person gets ONE personal link (no account) that holds the roles of all their places; it opens “My communities” (#/moje): a greeting, units with the role, what's new. Links are shown by the import and by the community's “People” tab; the link label contains no name.
